        "hypothesis": "Contiguous row pointers with valid restrict qualifiers expose independent stencil accesses to the compiler; an OpenMP SIMD reduction combines per-cell convergence tests without introducing loop-carried dependencies or changing the Jacobi sweep order.",
        "id": "a30d7c8d356e42e0",
        "ordinal": 1,
        "parent_id": null,
        "role": "B",
        "source_commits": [],
        "sources": [],
        "transformations": {
          "files": [
            "src/laplace_seq.c"
          ],
          "retained": [
            "Use local restricted row pointers for each source and destination row in the update and copy passes.",
            "Accumulate each row's convergence condition with a bitwise-OR SIMD reduction, then combine row flags into the existing hasError decision.",
            "Add SIMD to the independent interior-row copy loop and make the absolute-value helper inlineable."
          ]
        },
